  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The town of Hyères created a dog beach on Mérou beach, between L'Ayguade and Les Salins: a seaside area for dogs where owners can walk their dog and let it enjoy a swim. The area is marked off with ganivelle fencing, with clear signage.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Under the 2026 municipal beach regulation order (article 11), dogs are banned from the beaches, except guide dogs and specifically authorised areas, notably Mérou beach: so stay within the designated area. Le Var Tourisme states that the beach is open to dogs on a leash, with a shaded area of umbrella pines and a few tables. The town asks visitors to pick up after their dogs (bag dispensers are at the entrance) and notes that there is no beach shower in 2026 because of water restrictions. On the Vieux Salins coastal path and on the salt road closed to traffic, dogs must be on a leash.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: elsewhere in Hyères, don't assume a beach is open to dogs: the 2026 order bans them outside expressly authorised areas.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The <a href="/en/fiche-le-pradet-caniplouf">Cani Plouf in Le Pradet</a>, to the west, is another dog beach in the area.</p>
